  <h1>ALL ABOUT NITRO COLD BREW COFFEE</h1>
  <p>This is a historical informational page, kept as originally framed. It is general information and not medical advice.</p>

  <h2>What is nitro coffee?</h2>
  <p>A common question is: what is nitro cold brew? Nitro coffee is cold brew coffee infused with nitrogen gas and served on tap, which gives it a smooth, creamy texture.</p>

  <h2>Is nitro coffee bad for you?</h2>
  <p>A common question is: is nitro coffee bad for you, or is nitro cold brew bad for you? This historical page addresses it as general information only; it is not medical advice, so talk to a health professional about your own situation.</p>

  <h2>Nitro coffee versus traditional coffee</h2>
  <p>The page compares nitro coffee with traditional coffee, including a nutrition framing. It is kept as a historical comparison; talk to a health professional about your own situation.</p>

  <h2>Cold brew versus cold brewed</h2>
  <p>Cold brew is steeped in cold or room-temperature water. Coffee brewed hot and then chilled is cold brewed, which is a different thing.</p>

  <h2>Nitrogen, safety and quality</h2>
  <p>The page explains the role of nitrogen in serving and keeping nitro coffee, and how safety and quality are approached. Follow the instructions supplied with your equipment.</p>

  <h2>Kegs and dispensing equipment</h2>
  <p>Nitro coffee is kegged and served through dispensing equipment. See the current <a href="/kegerators/">equipment to serve nitro coffee</a> and <a href="/nitro-coffee-kegs/">nitro coffee kegs</a>.</p>

  <h2>Equipment maintenance</h2>
  <p>Keep faucets and lines clean as part of regular maintenance.</p>

  <h2>Changing kegs</h2>
  <p>When a keg is empty, disconnect it and connect a full one, following the supplier's instructions.</p>

  <h2>Nitrogen supply</h2>
  <p>Where a nitrogen tank is used, it needs to be refilled or exchanged. Ask your supplier about nitrogen supply.</p>

  <h2>Where can I get nitro coffee?</h2>
  <p>See <a href="/products/">our products</a> and <a href="/howtobuy/">how to buy</a>, or visit the <a href="https://www.nitrocoffee.store/">Bona Fide webstore</a>.</p>

  <h2>Serving, starting and organic questions</h2>
  <p>Further questions about serving nitro coffee, getting started and organic coffee are covered in <a href="/nitro-coffee-questions/">Nitro Coffee Questions</a>. A newer overview is at <a href="/nitro-cold-brew/">All About Nitro Cold Brew Coffee</a>.</p>
